1. GitHub Repo Banao Aur Code Push KaroLocal computer pe project folder mein: 'git init', 'git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repo.git', '.gitignore' file banao (usme node_modules, dist, .env likh do taki secrets/build files push na ho), phir 'git add .', 'git commit -m "initial commit"', 'git push -u origin main'. GitHub pe repo private rakhna (Settings → Create private repository).
2. VPS + CloudPanel Ready KaroHostinger se KVM 2 VPS purchase karo (agar abhi tak nahi kiya), OS template mein 'Ubuntu 24.04 with CloudPanel' select karo. hPanel se VPS IP address note karo. Browser mein https://VPS-IP:8443 khol ke CloudPanel admin login karo.
3. Node.js, pnpm, PM2, Git Install/Confirm KaroSSH se VPS mein login karo ('ssh root@VPS-IP'). Phir: nvm install karo aur Node 22 activate karo, 'npm install -g pnpm pm2' chalao Node.js aur PM2 (process manager) ko globally available banane ke liye. Git usually pre-installed hota hai Ubuntu mein, 'git --version' se confirm kar lo.
4. PostgreSQL Database Banao (Aur Backup Restore Karo Agar Hai)CloudPanel dashboard → Databases → Add Database, PostgreSQL select karo, DB name/user/password set karo, note kar lo. Agar tumhare paas pehle se koi backup .sql file hai, use SFTP se upload karke restore karo: 'psql "postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/dbname" -f backup.sql'. Naya project hai to ye step tab karna jab schema/migrations ready ho.
5. GitHub Se Project Clone KaroVPS pe SSH se site ke htdocs folder mein jao (jo CloudPanel site create karte waqt banega, step 6 mein), phir: 'git clone https://github.com/username/repo.git .' — agar repo private hai, GitHub Personal Access Token password ki jagah use karna hoga (GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens se bana sakte ho).
6. Dependencies Install, Env Vars Set, Build KaroProject root mein 'pnpm install' chalao. Phir environment variables set karo — CloudPanel Node.js site ke 'Environment Variables' section mein ya '.env' file bana ke: NODE_ENV=production, PORT, DATABASE_URL, SESSION_SECRET, TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=1, BASE_PATH=/. Sab set hone ke baad 'pnpm run build' chalao — ye backend (dist/index.mjs) aur frontend (dist/public) dono build karega.
7. CloudPanel Mein Node.js Site + Static Site Add KaroCloudPanel → Sites → Add Site → 'Create a Node.js Site': backend domain daalo, app path 'artifacts/api-server' set karo, start command 'node --enable-source-maps dist/index.mjs'. Phir dusra Site → 'Create a Static Site': main domain daalo, document root 'artifacts/supportdesk-web/dist/public' set karo. Static site ke Vhost tab mein '/api' proxy_pass rule add karo backend ke port pe (jo maine pehle exact Nginx config diya tha).
8. SSL Enable Karo Aur deploy.sh Setup KaroDono sites ke 'SSL/TLS' tab mein jao (domain DNS pehle se VPS IP pe point hona chahiye), 'New Let's Encrypt Certificate' create karo — free, auto-renew. Phir 'deploy.sh' script project root mein daalo, 'chmod +x deploy.sh' chalao. Ab future mein sirf 'git push' (local se) + 'bash deploy.sh' (server pe) se live update ho jayega.
  
Ye poora flow hai — GitHub push se lekar live site tak, sab 8 steps mein cover ho gaya, git clone approach ke saath (zip upload nahi).
**Order important hai** — step 5 (git clone) actually step 7 (Node.js site create) ke baad bhi ho sakta hai, kyunki CloudPanel site create karte waqt hi `htdocs` folder banta hai jahan clone karna hai. Practical order: **Step 2 → 3 → 7 (sites create karo pehle, empty) → 5 (clone) → 4 (DB) → 6 (build) → 8 (SSL+script)**. Card mein maine logical grouping ke hisaab se likha hai, but real terminal session mein thoda aage-peeche ho sakta hai — koi dikkat nahi. 
